1. First, determine the size of each container. Divide the total gallons of gas by the number of containers: 15 gallons / 5 containers = 3 gallons per container. 2. Next, calculate the amount of gas Josey needed in gallons: Josey needed 1/4 of a container, so she needed (1/4) * 3 gallons = 3/4 gallons. 3. Finally, convert gallons to pints. There are 8 pints in a gallon, so Josey needed (3/4) gallons * 8 pints/gallon = 6 pints.

So the answer is 6.
